From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: ICLRStrongName, StrongNameGetBlob(FromImage), StrongNameSignatureVerificationFromImage.

The .NET 4 way to the strong name functions is ICLRRuntimeInfo::GetInterface(CLSID_CLRStrongName,
IID_ICLRStrongName) (tools that sign or check assemblies, build tasks); it gave CLASS_E_CLASSNOTAVAILABLE.
Now it is an ICLRStrongName whose methods are the strong name functions with the error as the HRESULT
(StrongNameErrorInfo). StrongNameGetBlob and StrongNameGetBlobFromImage copy a file's or an image's bytes
(too small a buffer: the size needed); StrongNameSignatureVerificationFromImage verifies the signature of a
mapped image, laid out again as its file (headers and each section's raw data at its file offset). An image
from memory has no location, so an ECMA-keyed (framework) assembly is not trusted by where it lives.
include/metahost.idl: ICLRStrongName and CLSID_CLRStrongName as in dotnet/coreclr's metahost.idl (MIT).
